      "question_type": "MCQ",
      "question_text": "The radius of the Earth is 6400 km . If the height of an antenna is 500 m , then its range is",
      "question_html": "<div class=\"q-body\"> <div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->The radius of the Earth is 6400 km . If the height of an antenna is 500 m , then its range is\n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div></div>",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "800 km",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->800 km\n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "100 km",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->100 km\n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "80 km",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->80 km\n<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "10 km",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->10 km<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": null,
      "explanation_text": "To find the range of the antenna (i.e., the distance to the horizon), we can use the formula: $d=\\sqrt{2Rℎ}$ where: • $R$ is the radius of the Earth • $ℎ$ is the height of the antenna Since the Earth's radius is given as 6400 km and the antenna's height is 500 m, we first convert the height into kilometers: • $500\\text{m}=0.5\\text{km}$ Now, plug the values into the formula: $d=\\sqrt{2 \\times 6400 \\times 0.5}=\\sqrt{6400}=80\\text{km}$ Thus, the range of the antenna is 80 km, which corresponds to Option C.",
      "explanation_html": "<div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p>To find the range of the antenna (i.e., the distance to the horizon), we can use the formula:</p>\n<p> $d=\\sqrt{2Rℎ}$ </p>\n<p>where:  </p>\n<p>•  $R$  is the radius of the Earth  </p>\n<p>•  $ℎ$  is the height of the antenna</p>\n<p>Since the Earth's radius is given as 6400 km and the antenna's height is 500 m, we first convert the height into kilometers:</p>\n<p>•  $500\\text{m}=0.5\\text{km}$ </p>\n<p>Now, plug the values into the formula:</p>\n<p> $d=\\sqrt{2 \\times 6400 \\times 0.5}=\\sqrt{6400}=80\\text{km}$ </p>\n<p>Thus, the range of the antenna is 80 km, which corresponds to Option C.</p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>",
